# The kernel of a generic x86-64 PC: Alpine's long-term-support kernel, for real PCs
# (their storage, USB and graphics drivers as modules) and virtual machines alike.
linux-lts
# The firmware it loads for common PC hardware (decision 0016: published for
# redistribution, as locked distribution packages): GPUs (AMD, Intel i915 and xe), Intel
# Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, audio and more (intel), Wi-Fi and Bluetooth of Qualcomm Atheros
# (ath10k, ath11k, ath12k, qca), Realtek (rtw88, rtw89, rtlwifi, rtl_bt), Broadcom and
# Cypress (brcm, cypress) and MediaTek, Realtek's Ethernet (rtl_nic). Each provides
# linux-firmware-any, which linux-lts needs. scripts/kernel-package.sh moves them into
# the kernel's firmware/, with their licenses (the firmware-licenses-pc stage: the
# packages carry none). NVIDIA's (nouveau) is not among them yet.
linux-firmware-amdgpu
linux-firmware-i915
linux-firmware-xe
linux-firmware-intel
linux-firmware-ath10k
linux-firmware-ath11k
linux-firmware-ath12k
linux-firmware-rtw88
linux-firmware-rtw89
linux-firmware-rtlwifi
linux-firmware-rtl_bt
linux-firmware-rtl_nic
linux-firmware-brcm
linux-firmware-cypress
linux-firmware-mediatek
linux-firmware-qca
# CPU microcode: AMD's as firmware files (linux-firmware-amd-ucode) and as the early
# archive (amd-ucode), Intel's as its early archive (intel-ucode). The kernel loads
# microcode only early (CONFIG_MICROCODE_LATE_LOADING is off): the archives go into the
# kernel's microcode/, for the loader to put in front of the initramfs.
linux-firmware-amd-ucode
amd-ucode
intel-ucode
